{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/249123-demon-seed-collection-errata-thread","id":249123,"title":"Demon Seed Collection errata thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-04T13:49:14-07:00","id":249123,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Demon Seed Collection errata thread","content":"<i>The Demon Seed Collection</i> is out to Kickstarter backers. Please report typos and visual glitches here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: By the way, it sometimes takes a few hours for all the e-mails to send out. If you don't have it in the next few hours, check Rich's instructions in the <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition/posts/975331\" target=\"_blank\">Kickstarter update</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 09-04-2014, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T15:21:14-07:00","id":249205,"title":"","content":"Excellent! Would it be reasonable to get an estimate on how long we have until the thread closes? I (and probably others) missed the boat on Interface and Shattered City.<br /> <br /> I guess it comes down to whether it's more preferred to have lots of shorter posts or longer, neater posts. A more compiled post would seem to benefit from having a deadline to shoot for. Alternatively, we can just post them as we get to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1925-toroid","name":"Toroid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T15:28:03-07:00","id":249212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toroid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/249123-demon-seed-collection-errata-thread?p=249205#post249205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent! Would it be reasonable to get an estimate on how long we have until the thread closes? I (and probably others) missed the boat on Interface and Shattered City.<br /> <br /> I guess it comes down to whether it's more preferred to have lots of shorter posts or longer, neater posts. A more compiled post would seem to benefit from having a deadline to shoot for. Alternatively, we can just post them as we get to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Post them as you find them. It's pretty easy to read the threads and go through the issues as long as people cite properly and stay on topic. The thread will be open until September 12th. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T19:32:24-07:00","id":249392,"title":"","content":"Great! Thank you. Here's what I have so far.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing word</u> - Back cover. &quot;Go Hollywood&quot; should be &quot;Go to Hollywood&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Confusion</u> - p. 5 second to last paragraph under Sub Rosa: &quot;Whatever the goal of that plan was, it remains, as that Agency has long since dissolved.&quot; This sentence really threw me. Both &quot;that plan&quot; and &quot;it&quot; seem ambiguous. Rereading the sentences before it, I'm still not sure whether they refer to the ring's plan/goal or the Machine's. Secondly, the paragraph jumps from talking about &quot;a clever ring of demons&quot; to &quot;that Agency&quot; without telling readers if &amp; how the 2 groups are connected. Could be cleared up by just changing &quot;that Agency&quot; to &quot;that ring&quot;.<br /> <br /> <u>Verb Conjugation</u> - p. 5 below Agendas &gt; Inquisitors: &quot;...the residual effects of all those plots has left a virtual record...&quot; since &quot;effects&quot; is plural, it should be &quot;...the residual effects of all those plots <b>have</b> left a virtual record...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Missing character</u> - p. 6 under Agendas &gt; Tempters: &quot;...the Fatih or Beyo\u011flu districts...&quot; Though it shows here on the forum just fine, \u011f is an empty box in my pdf. Tried it on 2 computers, with different versions of Acrobat and got boxes both times.<br /> <br /> <u>Extra word?</u> - p. 7 in The Golden Gate paragraph: &quot;The building itself is a probability a matrix...&quot; maybe it should read &quot;The building itself is, in all probability, an occult matrix&quot; or (considering the rest of the sentence) &quot;The building itself is a probability matrix&quot; (It's a cool enough idea that it might even merit capitalizing Probability Matrix as a new term of demonic art.)<br /> <br /> <u>Hyphen</u> - p. 7 below Seed: Do Until Death &quot;required a mobster to make a split second decision&quot; needs a hyphen between &quot;split&quot; and &quot;second&quot; because it's a compound adjective here.<br /> <br /> <u>Capitalization inconsistency</u> - p.10 second sentence after Sub Rosa: &quot;Here demons can find copious amounts of abandoned infrastructure&quot; Interestingly, this is the only instance of Infrastructure in the whole book that isn't capitalized.<br /> <br /> <u>Capitalization of &quot;Cover&quot;</u> - Checked each instance of the word. Here are several instances where I suspect the term &quot;cover&quot; should possibly be capitalized to distinguish demonic and mundane usage.<br /> p. 5 bottom left of page &quot;mass cleansings of cover identities&quot;<br /> p. 7 top right of page &quot;Amid all this confusion, demons enjoy natural cover,&quot;<br /> p. 8 under Interchangeable Parts, paragraph 1: &quot;forming attachments or just using them as cover.&quot;<br /> p. 8 under Interchangeable Parts, paragraph 2: &quot;helping them establish the cover and connections needed to survive.&quot;<br /> p. 10 bottom right paragraph &quot;The Machine used this as helpful cover and obfuscation&quot;<br /> p. 14 under Interchangeable Parts, paragraph 2: &quot;places that visibly lower-class covers can\u2019t go at all.&quot;<br /> p. 16 Up Next &gt; Cold Calls: &quot;to a known human (or human cover identity) ring&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Extra word</u> - p. 29 &quot;especially the Stolen Generation, removed removed from their traditional families and ways.&quot; only needs one &quot;removed&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1925-toroid","name":"Toroid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T20:16:46-07:00","id":249417,"title":"","content":"Front Cover<br /> a <b>player</b> supplement<br /> should probably a storyteller supplement or left off altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/284-mason","name":"Mason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T19:34:25-07:00","id":254945,"title":"","content":"<u>Extra Word?</u> - p. 8 second paragraph after Infrastructure &quot;...crossing over often requires such a leap of faith in one direction or another to bypass their checkpoints.&quot; The phrase &quot;such a ____&quot; seems to set up for a &quot;that ___&quot; which never comes. Just dropping the &quot;such&quot; would seem to fix it.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing Word</u> - p. 9 Methods &gt; Cool Heads Prevail &quot;...can often be helpful masking demonic activity&quot; needs a &quot;with&quot; or an &quot;in&quot; between &quot;helpful&quot; &amp; &quot;masking&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Wrong Term</u> - p. 9 Methods &gt; Cool Heads Prevail &quot;...this Merit helps it disperse&quot; should be &quot;...this Embed helps it disperse&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Ambiguous Phrasing</u> - p. 10 just above Sub Rosa &quot;...bring in new tech and medically oriented businesses.&quot; The way I first read this was that they were bringing in new tech, and also medically oriented businesses. I think the intended meaning was was new tech oriented businesses and new medically oriented businesses. So to clarify, I would rewrite it as &quot;...bring in new tech- and medically-oriented businesses.&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Undefined Term</u> - p. 10 Just under Sub Rosa &quot;spider holes&quot; are mentioned. After reading the rest of the Baltimore section, I would guess spider holes would be boltholes that are tied into the Spiderweb using the optional rule on p. 15. As much as I like the term, &quot;spider holes&quot; is mysteriously never defined or even used elsewhere in the text. <br /> <br /> <u>Capitalization</u> - &quot;Tick-Tock Men&quot; seems to be capitalized more often than not, so here's a list of the handful of places it isn't capitalized.<br /> p. 11 top-left of the page &quot;...whether Infrastructure, angels, or tick-tock men.&quot;<br /> p. 11 Factions &gt; Dokutsu &quot;Dokutsu believes the tick-tock men are related...&quot;<br /> p. 12 Factions &gt; Vendetta &quot;Vendetta claims that the tick-tock menare tools...&quot;<br /> p. 12 Notable Characters &gt; The Tick-Tock Men: &quot;If you listen closely in the presence of a tick-tock man,...&quot;<br /> p. 12 Notable Characters &gt; The Tick-Tock Men: &quot;...taken by the tick-tock men,...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Space Missing</u> - p. 12 Factions &gt; Vendetta &quot;Vendetta claims that the tick-tock menare tools...&quot; Needs a space between &quot;men&quot; and &quot;are&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Hyphen Missing?</u> - p. 13 Locations &gt; Abandoned Row Houses: &quot;Many demons have dead drops here,...&quot; Of 3 instances of &quot;dead-drop&quot; in the book, this is the only one that isn't hyphenated.<br /> <br /> <u>Capitalization</u> - p. 15 Methods &gt; Crack Driver: &quot;merit&quot; isn't capitalized in the first sentence<br /> <br /> <u>Capitalization</u> - p. 15 Methods &gt; Pusher: &quot;merit&quot; isn't capitalized in the first sentence<br /> <br /> <u>Awkward Phrasing</u> - p. 15 last paragraph of the page: &quot;They will not inflict...within 24 hours.&quot; I feel like this should be 2 sentences because there are 2 separate ideas expressed. The first clause before the comma describes a conditional behavior that really has more to do with the beatings mentioned in the sentence before it. While, the latter part details a separate action they always carry out. Also, the &quot;within 24 hours&quot; part seems tacked on at an odd place. I suggest revising it to read &quot;...violently against them<b>. Within 24 hours, they</b> dump the character...&quot; and drop &quot;within 24 hours&quot; from the end of the sentence.<br /> <br /> <u>Capitalization toss-up</u> - p. 17 in the paragraph just above Agendas &quot;...tried to claim credit for the west coast rap scene;...&quot; It's kind of a judgement call, but I think &quot;west coast&quot; is supposed to be capitalized in this case. <br /> <br /> <u>Missing Hyphen</u> - p. 17 Agendas &gt; Inquisitors, Integrators &amp; Saboteurs: there are 5 instances of &quot;God Machine&quot; missing its hyphen.<br /> Inquisitors &quot;...behaviors desired by the God Machine?&quot;<br /> Inquisitors &quot;How does the God Machine plan out...&quot;<br /> Integrators &quot;...stories are also the God Machine\u2019s way...&quot;<br /> Saboteurs &quot;...decode the God Machine\u2019s mysterious ways...&quot;<br /> Saboteurs &quot;...competing on the God Machine\u2019s own turf.&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Capitalization</u> - p. 18 bottom left of page &quot;...they are difficult to tie back to the agency.&quot; This should probably be capitalized since it seems to refer to Agency in the demonic sense.<br /> <br /> <u>Extra Word</u> - p. 19 Locations &gt; the Home of the Unknown Star &quot;...the celebrity who once is lived here is never named.&quot; There's an extra &quot;is&quot; between &quot;once&quot; &amp; &quot;lived&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1925-toroid","name":"Toroid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T21:52:09-07:00","id":255047,"title":"","content":"<u>Missing hyphen</u>? - p. 20 Elements &gt; The Truth &quot;...inhuman connection to the God Machine.&quot; In the book, this is at the end of a line so it's kind of hard to tell if the hyphen is there or not.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing hyphens</u> - p. 28 &quot;God Machine&quot; missing its hyphens again.<br /> &quot;Of course, the God Machine is not synonymous...&quot;<br /> &quot;...equating the God Machine with prisoner importation,...&quot;<br /> &quot;...the God Machine wanted to run this program in isolation.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1925,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1925-toroid","user":"Toroid","date":".  fixed the page reference from 19 to 20 09-12-2014, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1925-toroid","name":"Toroid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T03:57:37-07:00","id":255185,"title":"","content":"<u>Misplaced Word?</u> - p. 20 just above Interchangeable Parts: &quot;While Marlow\u2019s Cover is aging, her fame and connections yet have a role to play in the Machine\u2019s plans.&quot; The order of the words sounds off to me. I can't think of a rule to cite, but I feel like it reads better as &quot;...her fame and connections have a role <b>yet</b> to play...&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Inconsistent format</u> - The Methods sections for Hollywood and Sydney include parenthetical markers to denote Embeds. I think it's actually a nice feature since I can't always keep the Embeds and new/updated Merits straight. However, having 2 of the cities use this format seems to break the pattern set by all the others. Were it me, I'd just add the parentheticals for Embeds to the sections that don't have them. No real harm done leaving it the way it is though.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Heading Error</u></b> - p. 32 just above &quot;Academics:...&quot; The &quot;Methods&quot; header is completely missing. I noticed it because the Methods bookmark was missing from the Sydney section, so be sure to add the bookmark along with the header.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1925-toroid","name":"Toroid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}